# Built pages and their inputs are regenerable (each folder's CLAUDE.md has the
# command) and large — artifacts/ is ~265 MB on disk, ~2 MB of it irreplaceable.
# Committed: sources, build scripts, notes, and every hand-authored layer.

# --- build products: the self-contained published pages ---
07-21_mcq_forced_choice/report.html
07-27_trait_excerpts/trait_excerpts_artifact.html
07-29_dose_open_flip_explorer/dose_open_flip_explorer.html
07-29_trait_alternation/trait_alternation.html
07-30_dose_open_v3/dose_open_v3_report.html
07-31_forced_opener_disavowal/forced_opener_report.html
07-31_user_turn_probe/report.html
08-27_chain_holds_digest/index.html
# (07-28_cot_unfaithfulness/index.html and 07-30_salieri_switching/index.html
#  are covered by those folders' own .gitignore, which explain themselves.)

# --- payloads: gzip+base64 blobs regenerated by prepare_data.py ---
07-21_mcq_forced_choice/data.json
07-31_user_turn_probe/report_data.json
07-31_forced_opener_disavowal/flip_set.json

# 07-30_salieri_switching/report_artifact.html (6.8 MB) is a build product too,
# but it was committed back in 9f7fff1 and gitignore doesn't apply to tracked
# files. Untracking it is a separate call — it's already in history either way.

# --- extracted corpora: re-derived from logs/ by the extract_*.py scripts ---
corpus_*.jsonl
07-30_dose_open_v3/cell_dumps/
07-30_dose_open_v3/outtakes_full.json
07-29_trait_alternation/data/raw_exports/
07-29_trait_alternation/data/consolidated.json

# --- keep the hand-authored layers that live under an ignored data/ dir ---
# The root .gitignore has a blanket `**/data/`; these labelings are the one thing
# in here that cannot be regenerated, so they are re-included explicitly.
!07-29_trait_alternation/data/
07-29_trait_alternation/data/*
!07-29_trait_alternation/data/stances*.json
!07-29_trait_alternation/data/to_classify*.json
!07-29_trait_alternation/data/provenance2.json
